# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Environment / secrets. Any .env variant (.env.production, .env.local) stays
# local; only the example file, which holds no real values, is committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Local data. SQLite also writes -journal, -wal and -shm files next to the
# database, holding the same data.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
media/

# Test and coverage output
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Claude Code's per-machine settings. This machine's global gitignore already
# covers it; listed here so a clone anywhere else ignores it too.
.claude/settings.local.json
# Claude Code's worktrees: separate checkouts of this repository, each on its
# own branch, that background sessions work in. Their commits reach the repo
# through those branches, never as files here.
.claude/worktrees/

# Tailwind standalone binary (downloaded by scripts/tailwind.sh)
bin/

# Owner's personal reference notes, kept on the local machine only.
# Not part of the deliverable; see docs/ for the project documentation.
docs/LEARNING_GUIDE.md
docs/CI_CD_GUIDE.md
docs/CODEBASE_MAP.md

# Sprint reviews and retrospectives: the owner's written reflection, drafted
# here and submitted through the course LMS. The sprint plans stay committed.
docs/sprints/local/

# Original watch photography, straight off the camera. The finished photos are
# public, but the originals aren't the same files: they carry the phone's GPS
# location in their metadata, and Git keeps every byte of every version
# forever. Photos reach the site through the upload pipeline, which strips the
# metadata and makes the web sizes (#28, #68). The logos in design/logo/ stay
# committed: they're small, already public, and build_brand_assets.py needs them.
design/photos/
